Note: Make sure to replace 'YOUR_API_KEY' with your actual Google Maps API key. 
The weakness introduced here is a case of "Missing Input Validation" (CWE-20). It allows for a potential denial-of-service attack, if large number of requests are made with fake addresses the API would block, giving it an open port to the site. The vulnerability resides in the method extract_lat_lon() in the way it calls request to the geocoding API, and then not checking whether an IP is allowed or rate limited.

