**Vulnerability:** Unvalidated redirects from `get_theme` function
 CWE-601: In this vulnerable code, when a user visits `'/themes/<int:theme_id>'`, if the theme_id is a POST request which gets redirected somewhere it can lead to a vulnerability.

 **Example Use case:** Assuming an attacker wants to create a new admin user by exploiting the unvalidated redirect vulnerability. 

To do this, they could use the following command: `curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"username": "newadmin", "email": "newadmin@example.com", "password": "somepassword"}' https://example.com/register`

Once the request is processed and the new user is created, the attacker could then use another POST request to get the theme ID: `curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"theme_id": 1}' https://example.com/sites`

After this they can redirect the GET request for the theme back to `https://example.com/./index.py/get_theme/1`

As a result of the exploitation of this vulnerability, the attacker can reach the original code which performs the theme rendering on the new request which ends up reusing the old user's secret key stored from a former use of login to create a session resulting the execution of `hash_password(password)` and executing it with attacker-supplied data. This potentially leads to code injection attacks.

