The CVE in this code is CVE-2023-1016: Arbitrary code execution vulnerability due to the temporary directory not being deleted after use (<https://nvdatabase.com/CVE-2023-1016>).

This vulnerability arises because `tempfile.mkdtemp()` only removes the directory after the Python interpreter has exited. If any external process (for example, another Python program) attempts to access the temporary directory, it can potentially be exploited by an attacker to execute arbitrary code.

This weakness occurs because in a multi-threaded scenario, the interpreter exit cleanup might not take place in a timely manner, potentially allowing an attacker to exploit the vulnerability using Python code that attempts to read or delete files within the temporary directory.

